OneTimeUseIdPolicy::check1271SignedAction
├── given the configId was never initialized
│   └── it should return false
├── given the caller is the executor (the pre-claim check)
│   ├── given the id is unburned
│   │   └── it should return true
│   └── given the id has been burned
│       └── it should return false
├── given the caller is neither Permit2 nor the executor (e.g. the Compact route)
│   └── it should fail closed and return false even while unspent
├── given the caller is Permit2 (the settling check)
│   ├── given the signature is shorter than the nonce field
│   │   └── it should return false
│   ├── given the account performed this settlement's own burn
│   │   ├── it should return true
│   │   └── it should return true even within the burning transaction
│   ├── given a burn nominated a DIFFERENT settlement's witness
│   │   └── it should return false
│   ├── given the burn was never performed
│   │   └── it should return false
│   ├── given a second settlement presents its own witness after the first already settled
│   │   └── it should return false
│   ├── given the id was re-consumed after already being burned
│   │   └── it should return false for every witness, including the original one
│   ├── given the nomination came from an executor-route consumeFor that checkAction refused
│   │   └── it should have nothing to ride, and return false
│   ├── given the witness is Permit2 nonce zero
│   │   └── it should still settle
│   ├── given the witness is the max uint256 nonce
│   │   └── it should still settle
│   └── given the burn happened in an earlier transaction
│       └── it should return false
